        content: "To understand how the annuity formula translates into real-world wealth accumulation, let us trace a concrete, reproducible investment scenario.\n\nScenario Specifications:\n\u2022 Monthly Investment (P): \u20b910,000\n\u2022 Expected Annual Return (R): 12.0% per annum\n\u2022 Investment Tenure (T): 10 years (n = 120 monthly installments)\n\u2022 Total Out-of-Pocket Contribution: 120 \u00d7 \u20b910,000 = \u20b912,00,000\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the monthly interest rate (r)\nr = (12 / 100) / 12 = 0.01\n\n### Step 2: Compute the growth factor (1 + r)^n\n(1 + 0.01)^120 = (1.01)^120 \u2248 3.30038689\n\n### Step 3: Evaluate the annuity factor [((1 + r)^n - 1) / r]\n(3.30038689 - 1) / 0.01 = 2.30038689 / 0.01 = 230.038689\n\n### Step 4: Multiply by the monthly contribution and the beginning-of-period factor\nM = \u20b910,000 \u00d7 230.038689 \u00d7 1.01\nM = \u20b910,000 \u00d7 232.339076 = \u20b923,23,391\n\nAnalysis of the Compounding Result:\nOver 10 years, an investor contributes \u20b912,00,000 in principal. The final estimated maturity value is \u20b923,23,391. Of this total, \u20b911,23,391 (48.35% of the total portfolio value) consists purely of accumulated compound returns. The table below illustrates how the wealth accumulation accelerates exponentially across the timeline:\n\n| Milestone | Cumulative Invested Capital | Estimated Portfolio Value (12%) | Accumulated Capital Gain | Share of Gains in Total Wealth |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Year 1 (Month 12) | \u20b91,20,000 | \u20b91,28,093 | \u20b98,093 | 6.3% |\n| Year 3 (Month 36) | \u20b93,60,000 | \u20b94,35,076 | \u20b975,076 | 17.3% |\n| Year 5 (Month 60) | \u20b96,00,000 | \u20b98,24,864 | \u20b92,24,864 | 27.3% |\n| Year 7 (Month 84) | \u20b98,40,000 | \u20b913,44,726 | \u20b95,04,726 | 37.5% |\n| Year 10 (Month 120) | \u20b912,00,000 | \u20b923,23,391 | \u20b911,23,391 | 48.4% |\n| Year 15 (Month 180) | \u20b918,00,000 | \u20b950,45,760 | \u20b932,45,760 | 64.3% |\n| Year 20 (Month 240) | \u20b924,00,000 | \u20b999,91,479 | \u20b975,91,479 | 76.0% |\n\nNotice how between Year 10 and Year 20, the investor contributes an additional \u20b912,00,000, yet the total portfolio jumps by more than \u20b976,00,000. This non-linear explosion demonstrates why investment longevity far outweighs initial capital size."
